# WardenX — Docker build-context excludes (TASK-040F). Mirrors .gitignore's secret-file glob
# (never let a real .env/.env.bak.* reach a build context or layer) plus build artifacts (regenerable
# via `bun install`/`tsc -b`) and content that adds nothing to a running API/worker image.

.git/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# TypeScript project-reference build output — regenerable, and the image runs Bun over source
# directly (no compile step for the backend).
dist/
**/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets — anything starting with .env except the committed template. Same load-bearing glob as
# .gitignore: a bare `.env`/`.env.local` exclusion once missed a real `.env.bak.<epoch>` file that
# had live secrets sitting in the working tree.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor/AI-tool local state — never needed at runtime, and not something a build context should
# ever bundle into an image layer.
.vscode/
.claude/
.agents/
.codex/
.cursor/
.DS_Store

# Docs/spec corpus and point-in-time audit reports — large, and irrelevant to a running process.
docs/
audit/

# Coverage/test output.
coverage/
*.log
